/-!
# Complete intersections at a prime, and local complete intersections

Let `k` be a field and let `S` be a finite type `k`-algebra. This file proves that being a
complete intersection over `k` is a *local* condition on `Spec S` which can be tested on any
single presentation, and that a local complete intersection is exactly an algebra all of whose
local rings are complete intersections.

For a prime `q ⊆ S` the following are equivalent:

1. the local ring `S_q` is a complete intersection over `k`;
2. `S_g` is a local complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∈ S`, `g ∉ q`;
3. `S_g` is a global complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∈ S`, `g ∉ q`;
4. for every presentation `S = k[x_i]/I` in finitely many variables, with `q' ⊆ k[x_i]` the prime
   corresponding to `q`, the equivalent conditions (1)-(5) of Stacks 00SC hold; for instance the
   ideal `I_{q'}` of `k[x_i]_{q'}` is generated by a regular sequence.

Consequently `S` is a local complete intersection over `k` if and only if every local ring of `S`
is a complete intersection over `k`, and already if and only if every localization of `S` at a
maximal ideal is. Finally, for a local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type, being a complete
intersection can be tested on any surjection from a regular local `k`-algebra essentially of
finite type.

## Main results

* `IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae_generators`: the equivalence of (1)-(4), with
  item (4) stated both for all five conditions of 00SC together and for each one separately.
* `IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae`: the equivalence of (1)-(3) with item (4) in
  the form of condition (5) of 00SC, `I_{q'}` generated by a regular sequence.
* `IsLocalCompleteIntersection.tfae`: `S` is a local complete intersection over `k` if and only
  if every local ring of `S` is a complete intersection over `k`, if and only if every
  localization of `S` at a maximal ideal is.
* `IsCompleteIntersection.tfae`: for a local `k`-algebra `S` essentially of finite type, `S` is a
  complete intersection over `k` if and only if the kernel of every surjection onto `S` from a
  regular local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type is generated by a regular sequence, if and
  only if some such kernel is generated by `dim R - dim S` elements, if and only if `S` is a
  localization at a prime of a global, resp. local, complete intersection over `k`.
* `isLocalCompleteIntersection_iff_forall_isMaximal`: being a local complete intersection is a
  condition at the closed points.
* `Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq`: the codimension of a presentation at a prime
  exists, `height q' = height q + c` for some `c : ℕ`.
* `IsLocalCompleteIntersection.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection` and
  `IsGlobalCompleteIntersection.isLocalCompleteIntersection`: the two elementary comparisons of
  global and local complete intersections.

## Implementation notes

The local rings are abstract localizations. `Sq` is any `S`-algebra localizing `S` at `q`, its
`k`-algebra structure pinned to the one coming from `S` by `IsScalarTower k S Sq`, so a caller may
use whichever model is at hand. The localizations `S_g` are the construction `Localization.Away g`.

Item (4) quantifies over presentations in an arbitrary universe: `ι` ranges over `Type w` and the
localization `A` of `k[x_i]` over `Type (max u w)`, the universe of `MvPolynomial ι k` itself.

## References

* [StacksProject 00SG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SG), Lemma 10.135.8.
* [StacksProject 00SH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SH), Lemma 10.135.9.
* [StacksProject 00SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SF)
* [StacksProject 00SC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SC), Lemma 10.135.4, here
  `Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away`.
* [StacksProject 00SE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SE), Lemma 10.135.6, here
  `IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae`.
* [StacksProject 00QS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QS), Lemma 10.126.7, here
  `Algebra.FinitePresentation.exists_algEquiv_localizationAway_of_algEquiv_atPrime`.
* [StacksProject 00S9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00S9), Definition 10.135.1, here
  `IsGlobalCompleteIntersection` and `IsLocalCompleteIntersection`.
* [StacksProject 00SD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00SD), Definition 10.135.5, here
  `IsCompleteIntersection`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u u₂ v w
open RingTheory.Sequence IsLocalRing

/-! ### Localizations -/

namespace CompleteIntersection

/-- A local ring that is a localization of `T` at a submonoid `M` is the localization of `T` at
the prime lying under its maximal ideal. -/
theorem isLocalization_primeCompl_under {T : Type*} [CommRing T] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra T S] [IsLocalRing S] (M : Submonoid T) (hM : IsLocalization M S) :
    IsLocalization ((maximalIdeal S).comap (algebraMap T S)).primeCompl S := by
  have := hM
  refine IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_is_exists_mul_mem S M _ (fun m hm ↦ ?_) (fun x ↦ ?_)
  · exact notMem_maximalIdeal.mpr (IsLocalization.map_units S ⟨m, hm⟩)
  · have hx : IsUnit (algebraMap T S (x : T)) := notMem_maximalIdeal.mp x.2
    obtain ⟨⟨y, s⟩, e⟩ := IsLocalization.surj M (↑hx.unit⁻¹ : S)
    have key : algebraMap T S ((x : T) * y) = algebraMap T S s := by
      have :
        algebraMap T S (x : T) * (↑hx.unit⁻¹ * algebraMap T S s) =
          algebraMap T S (x : T) * algebraMap T S y := by
        rw [e]
      rw [← mul_assoc] at this
      simpa [hx.unit_spec] using this.symm
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (IsLocalization.eq_iff_exists M S).mp key
    exact
      ⟨c * y, by
        rw [mul_comm ((c : T) * y) (x : T), ← mul_assoc, mul_comm (x : T) (c : T), mul_assoc, hc];
        exact mul_mem c.2 s.2⟩

/-- `IsLocalization` read through an isomorphism of the base ring. -/
theorem isLocalization_comap_of_ringEquiv {T T₀ : Type*} [CommRing T] [CommRing T₀] {B : Type*}
    [CommRing B] [Algebra T₀ B] [Algebra T B] (e : T ≃+* T₀)
    (he : ∀ x, algebraMap T₀ B (e x) = algebraMap T B x) (M : Submonoid T₀) [IsLocalization M B] :
    IsLocalization (Submonoid.comap (e : T →+* T₀) M) B
    where
  map_units y := by
    rw [← he]
    exact IsLocalization.map_units B ⟨e y, y.2⟩
  surj z := by
    obtain ⟨⟨x, s⟩, hx⟩ := IsLocalization.surj M z
    refine ⟨⟨e.symm x, ⟨e.symm s, ?_⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    · simp
    · simpa [← he] using hx
  exists_of_eq {x y} hxy := by
    rw [← he, ← he] at hxy
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (IsLocalization.eq_iff_exists M B).mp hxy
    refine ⟨⟨e.symm c, ?_⟩, e.injective ?_⟩
    · simp
    · simpa using hc

/-- A local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type over `k` is the localization at a prime of a
quotient of a polynomial ring over `k`. -/
@[ega "IV 1.3.11" "base ring is a field"]
theorem exists_finiteType_isLocalization_atPrime (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v) [CommRing S]
    [Algebra k S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (J : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k)) (_ : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ J) S) (_
      : IsScalarTower k (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ J) S) (p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ J)) (_
      : p.IsPrime), IsLocalization.AtPrime S p := by
  obtain ⟨n, F, hF⟩ :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial''.mp
      (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType k (Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra k S))
  let T := MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ RingHom.ker F
  let e : T ≃ₐ[k] Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra k S := Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hF
  let algTS : Algebra T S :=
    ((algebraMap (Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra k S) S).comp (e : T →+* _)).toAlgebra
  have he :
    ∀ x : T, algebraMap (Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra k S) S (e x) = algebraMap T S x :=
    fun x ↦ rfl
  have hts : ∀ x : k, algebraMap k S x = algebraMap T S (algebraMap k T x) := by
    intro x
    rw [← he, AlgEquiv.commutes]
    exact IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra k S) S x
  have : IsScalarTower k T S := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq hts
  have hloc :=
    isLocalization_comap_of_ringEquiv (T₀ := Algebra.EssFiniteType.subalgebra k S) (B := S) (T :=
      T) (e : T ≃+* _) he (Algebra.EssFiniteType.submonoid k S)
  exact
    ⟨n, RingHom.ker F, algTS, inferInstance, (maximalIdeal S).comap (algebraMap T S),
      inferInstance, isLocalization_primeCompl_under _ hloc⟩

/-- A local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type over `k` is a quotient of a localization of a
polynomial ring over `k` at a prime. -/
@[ega "IV 1.3.11" "base ring is a field"]
theorem exists_atPrime_surjective (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v) [CommRing S] [Algebra k S]
    [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (q : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k)) (_ : q.IsPrime) (f :
      Localization.AtPrime q →ₐ[k] S), Function.Surjective f := by
  obtain ⟨n, J, algTS, twr, p, hp, hL⟩ := exists_finiteType_isLocalization_atPrime k S
  set P₀ := MvPolynomial (Fin n) k with hP₀
  set T := P₀ ⧸ J with hT
  have hgs : Function.Surjective (algebraMap P₀ T) := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  set q : Ideal P₀ := p.comap (algebraMap P₀ T) with hq
  have hqp : q.IsPrime := inferInstance
  have hmap : Submonoid.map (algebraMap P₀ T) q.primeCompl = p.primeCompl := by
    ext x
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
      exact hy
    · intro hx
      obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hgs x
      exact ⟨y, hx, rfl⟩
  have : IsLocalization (Submonoid.map (algebraMap P₀ T) q.primeCompl) S := by
    rw [hmap]; exact hL
  refine
    ⟨n, q, hqp,
      {
        IsLocalization.map (S := Localization.AtPrime q) S (algebraMap P₀ T)
          (Submonoid.le_comap_map (S := q.primeCompl) (f := algebraMap P₀ T)) with
        commutes' := ?_ },
      ?_⟩
  · intro r
    change
      IsLocalization.map (S := Localization.AtPrime q) S (algebraMap P₀ T)
          (Submonoid.le_comap_map (S := q.primeCompl) (f := algebraMap P₀ T))
          (algebraMap k (Localization.AtPrime q) r) =
        algebraMap k S r
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k P₀ (Localization.AtPrime q) r, IsLocalization.map_eq, ←
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k P₀ T r, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k T S r]
  · exact IsLocalization.map_surjective_of_surjective q.primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime q) S hgs

/-- `RingHom.ker` of a `k`-algebra map and of its underlying ring map are the same ideal. -/
theorem ker_coe_algHom {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] {A : Type*}
    [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] (f : A →ₐ[k] S) : RingHom.ker ((f : A →+* S)) = RingHom.ker f := by
  ext x; simp [RingHom.mem_ker]

/-- `RingHom.ker` of a composite of `k`-algebra maps and of the composite of the underlying ring
maps are the same ideal. -/
theorem ker_comp_coe_algHom {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S]
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra k A] [Algebra k B] (f : B →ₐ[k] S)
    (ψ : A →ₐ[k] B) : RingHom.ker ((f : B →+* S).comp (ψ : A →+* B)) = RingHom.ker (f.comp ψ) := by
  ext x; simp [RingHom.mem_ker]

/-- Given a `k`-algebra `T` with a prime `p` and a localization `Sq` of `T` at `p`, and an element
`h ∉ p`, the localization `T_h` is again a `k`-algebra having `Sq` as a localization at a prime. -/
theorem exists_isLocalization_atPrime_localizationAway {k : Type u} [Field k] {T : Type*}
    [CommRing T] [Algebra k T] {Sq : Type*} [CommRing Sq] [Algebra k Sq] [Algebra T Sq]
    [IsScalarTower k T Sq] (p : Ideal T) [p.IsPrime] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq p] {h : T}
    (hh : h ∉ p) :
    ∃ (_ : Algebra (Localization.Away h) Sq) (_ : IsScalarTower k (Localization.Away h) Sq) (p' :
      Ideal (Localization.Away h)) (_ : p'.IsPrime), IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq p' := by
  have hloc : IsLocalRing Sq := IsLocalization.AtPrime.isLocalRing Sq p
  have hgu : ∀ y : Submonoid.powers h, IsUnit (algebraMap T Sq (y : T)) := by
    rintro ⟨y, m, rfl⟩
    simpa using (IsLocalization.map_units (M := p.primeCompl) Sq ⟨h, hh⟩).pow m
  let algL : Algebra (Localization.Away h) Sq :=
    (IsLocalization.lift (M := Submonoid.powers h) hgu).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower T (Localization.Away h) Sq :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x ↦
      (RingHom.congr_fun (IsLocalization.lift_comp hgu) x).symm
  have : IsScalarTower k (Localization.Away h) Sq :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x ↦ by
      rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k T (Localization.Away h) x, ←
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply T (Localization.Away h) Sq, ←
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k T Sq]
  have hSloc :
    IsLocalization (Submonoid.map (algebraMap T (Localization.Away h)) p.primeCompl) Sq :=
    IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_submonoid_le (Localization.Away h) Sq (Submonoid.powers h)
      p.primeCompl (Submonoid.powers_le.mpr hh)
  exact
    ⟨algL, inferInstance, (maximalIdeal Sq).comap (algebraMap (Localization.Away h) Sq),
      inferInstance, isLocalization_primeCompl_under _ hSloc⟩

/-- For a surjection `R ↠ S`, a prime `q ⊆ S` and a localization `A` of `R` at `q' = q ∩ R`, the
natural map `A → S_q` is a surjection of `k`-algebras with kernel `(Ker(R → S))·A`. In other words
`A/(Ker(R → S))·A` is the local ring `S_q`. -/
theorem exists_surjective_algHom_ker_eq_map_ker {k : Type u} [Field k] {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [Algebra k R] {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra R S] [IsScalarTower k R S]
    (hf : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R S)) (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (A : Type*) [CommRing A]
    [Algebra R A] [Algebra k A] [IsScalarTower k R A]
    [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap R S))] (Sq : Type*) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq]
    [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] [Algebra k Sq] [IsScalarTower k S Sq] :
    ∃ θ : A →ₐ[k] Sq,
      Function.Surjective θ ∧
        RingHom.ker θ = (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R S)).map (algebraMap R A) := by
  set q' := q.comap (algebraMap R S) with hq'
  set g : R →+* Sq := (algebraMap S Sq).comp (algebraMap R S) with hg
  have hgS : ∀ x : R, g x = algebraMap S Sq (algebraMap R S x) := fun x ↦ rfl
  have hgu : ∀ y : q'.primeCompl, IsUnit (g y) := fun y ↦
    IsLocalization.map_units (M := q.primeCompl) Sq ⟨algebraMap R S y, y.2⟩
  set θ₀ : A →+* Sq := IsLocalization.lift (M := q'.primeCompl) hgu with hθ₀
  have hcomp : ∀ x : R, θ₀ (algebraMap R A x) = g x := fun x ↦
    RingHom.congr_fun (IsLocalization.lift_comp hgu) x
  have hmk : ∀ (r : R) (u : q'.primeCompl), g r = g (u : R) * θ₀ (IsLocalization.mk' A r u) :=
    fun r u ↦ (IsLocalization.lift_mk'_spec hgu r _ u).mp rfl
  refine ⟨{ θ₀ with commutes' := fun r ↦ ?_ }, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [show (algebraMap k A) r = algebraMap R A (algebraMap k R r) from
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k R A r]
    change θ₀ (algebraMap R A (algebraMap k R r)) = _
    rw [hcomp, hgS, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k R S, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k S Sq]
  · intro z
    obtain ⟨⟨s, t⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective q.primeCompl z
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hf s
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hf (t : S)
    have hu' : u ∈ q'.primeCompl := by
      simp only [hq', Ideal.mem_primeCompl_iff, Ideal.mem_comap, hu]
      exact t.2
    refine ⟨IsLocalization.mk' A r ⟨u, hu'⟩, ?_⟩
    have h1 := hmk r ⟨u, hu'⟩
    rw [hgS, hgS, hu, hr] at h1
    change θ₀ (IsLocalization.mk' A r ⟨u, hu'⟩) = IsLocalization.mk' Sq s t
    rw [eq_comm, IsLocalization.mk'_eq_iff_eq_mul, h1, mul_comm]
  · refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · intro a ha
      rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at ha
      obtain ⟨⟨r, u⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective q'.primeCompl a
      have ha' : θ₀ (IsLocalization.mk' A r u) = 0 := ha
      have hgr : g r = 0 := by rw [hmk r u, ha', mul_zero]
      rw [hgS] at hgr
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff q.primeCompl Sq _).mp hgr
      obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hf (c : S)
      have hw' : w ∈ q'.primeCompl := by
        simp only [hq', Ideal.mem_primeCompl_iff, Ideal.mem_comap, hw]
        exact c.2
      have hwr : w * r ∈ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R S) := by
        rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_mul, hw]
        exact hc
      obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ : IsUnit (algebraMap R A w) := IsLocalization.map_units A ⟨w, hw'⟩
      have hru : algebraMap R A r ∈ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R S)).map (algebraMap R A) := by
        have h2 :=
          (Ideal.map (algebraMap R A) (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R S))).mul_mem_left (↑v⁻¹ : A)
            (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap R A) hwr)
        rw [map_mul, ← hv, ← mul_assoc] at h2
        simpa using h2
      obtain ⟨v', hv'⟩ : IsUnit (algebraMap R A (u : R)) := IsLocalization.map_units A u
      have h3 :=
        (Ideal.map (algebraMap R A) (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R S))).mul_mem_left (↑v'⁻¹ : A) hru
      rw [← IsLocalization.mk'_spec' A r u, ← hv', ← mul_assoc] at h3
      simpa using h3
    · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
      intro x hx
      rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
      change θ₀ (algebraMap R A x) = 0
      rw [hcomp, hgS, RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx, map_zero]

end CompleteIntersection

/-! ### Global and local complete intersections -/

/-- A global complete intersection over `k` is a local one, the covering family being `{1}`. -/
theorem IsGlobalCompleteIntersection.isLocalCompleteIntersection {k : Type u} [Field k] {A : Type*}
    [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] (hA : IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k A) :
    IsLocalCompleteIntersection k A :=
  ⟨{1}, by simp, fun g hg ↦ by
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hg
    exact hg ▸ isGlobalCompleteIntersection_localization k A 1 hA⟩

/-- In a local complete intersection `A` over `k`, every proper ideal misses some `g` with `A_g` a
global complete intersection over `k`. -/
theorem IsLocalCompleteIntersection.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection {k : Type u}
    [Field k] {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] (hA : IsLocalCompleteIntersection k A)
    {p : Ideal A} (hp : p ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ g ∉ p, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g) := by
  obtain ⟨s, hspan, hgci⟩ := hA
  have hex : ∃ g ∈ s, g ∉ p := by
    by_contra hc
    refine hp (top_le_iff.mp (hspan ▸ Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_))
    intro g hg
    by_contra hgp
    exact hc ⟨g, hg, hgp⟩
  obtain ⟨g, hgs, hgp⟩ := hex
  exact ⟨g, hgp, hgci g hgs⟩

/-- A surjection onto `S` from a regular local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type over `k`
whose kernel is generated by a regular sequence exhibits `S` as a complete intersection over
`k`. -/
theorem isCompleteIntersection_of_ker_eq_ofList {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra k S] {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType k A] {f : A →ₐ[k] S} (hf : Function.Surjective f) {rs : List A}
    (hrs : IsRegular A rs) (hker : Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker f) :
    IsCompleteIntersection k S := by
  refine
    ⟨A, ‹CommRing A›, ‹Algebra k A›, ‹IsRegularLocalRing A›, ‹Algebra.EssFiniteType k A›, rs, hrs,
      ⟨?_⟩⟩
  exact
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hf).symm.trans (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq k hker.symm)

/-! ### The codimension of a presentation at a prime -/

/-- For a presentation `S = k[x_i]/I` in finitely many variables and a prime `q ⊆ S`, the
corresponding prime `q'` of `k[x_i]` has finite height at least that of `q`, so the codimension
`c` with `height q' = height q + c` exists. -/
theorem Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra k S] {ι : Type w} [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (q : Ideal S)
    [q.IsPrime] : ∃ c : ℕ, (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c := by
  set q' := q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S) with hq'
  have hq'p : q'.IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  have hnoeth : IsNoetherianRing P.Ring := inferInstanceAs (IsNoetherianRing (MvPolynomial ι k))
  have hAnoeth : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime q') :=
    IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing q'.primeCompl _ hnoeth
  have hd : ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q') = (q'.height : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height q' _
  have hdq :
    ringKrullDim
        ((Localization.AtPrime q') ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring (Localization.AtPrime q'))) =
      (q.height : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ringKrullDim_quotient_map_ker_eq_height (algebraMap P.Ring S) P.algebraMap_surjective q _
  obtain ⟨d, hdd⟩ : ∃ d : ℕ, ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q') = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    obtain ⟨d, hd'⟩ :=
      ENat.ne_top_iff_exists.1
        (Ideal.height_ne_top_of_isPrime (I := maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q')))
    exact
      ⟨d, by
        rw [← IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim, ← hd']; rfl⟩
  have hheq : q'.height = (d : ℕ∞) := by exact_mod_cast hd.symm.trans hdd
  have hle : q.height ≤ (d : ℕ∞) := by
    have h1 : (q.height : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      rw [← hdq, ← hdd]; exact ringKrullDim_quotient_le _
    exact_mod_cast h1
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ :=
    ENat.ne_top_iff_exists.1
      (show q.height ≠ ⊤ from fun h => by
        rw [h] at hle; simp at hle)
  refine ⟨d - m, ?_⟩
  rw [← hm] at hle
  have hmd : m ≤ d := by exact_mod_cast hle
  rw [hheq, ← hm]
  exact_mod_cast (show d = m + (d - m) by omega)

/-! ### Spreading a global complete intersection out from a local ring -/

namespace CompleteIntersection

/-- If the local ring `S_q` of a finite type `k`-algebra `S` at a
prime `q` is also the local ring at a prime of a *global* complete intersection `B` over `k`, then
`S_g` is a global complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∉ q`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_of_atPrime {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v}
    [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (Sq : Type*)
    [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] [Algebra k Sq]
    [IsScalarTower k S Sq] {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [Algebra B Sq]
    [IsScalarTower k B Sq] (b : Ideal B) [b.IsPrime] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq b]
    (hB : IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k B) :
    ∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g) := by
  have hBft : Algebra.FiniteType k B := IsGlobalCompleteIntersection.finiteType k hB
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation k B := Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType.mp hBft
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation k S := Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType.mp ‹_›
  obtain ⟨g₁, hg₁, g, hg, ⟨e⟩⟩ :=
    Algebra.FinitePresentation.exists_algEquiv_localizationAway_of_algEquiv_atPrime b q Sq Sq
      (AlgEquiv.refl (R := k) (A₁ := Sq))
  exact ⟨g, hg, gci_transport k e (isGlobalCompleteIntersection_localization k B g₁ hB)⟩

/-- A surjection from a localization `k[y_1, …, y_m]_𝔭` of a polynomial ring onto a local ring `Sq`
presents `Sq` as the local ring at a prime `p` of a finite type `k`-algebra `T` generated by `m`
elements, the kernel of the surjection being generated by the kernel of the presentation. -/
private theorem exists_generators_isLocalization_atPrime_of_surjective {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {m : ℕ} {𝔭 : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)} [𝔭.IsPrime] {Sq : Type*} [CommRing Sq]
    [Algebra k Sq] [IsLocalRing Sq] (F : Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 →ₐ[k] Sq)
    (hF : Function.Surjective F) :
    ∃ (T : Type u) (_ : CommRing T) (_ : Algebra k T) (_ : Algebra.FiniteType k T)
      (_ : Algebra T Sq) (_ : IsScalarTower k T Sq) (p : Ideal T) (_ : p.IsPrime)
      (_ : IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq p) (P : Algebra.Generators k T (Fin m))
      (_ : IsLocalization.AtPrime (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) (p.comap (algebraMap P.Ring T))),
      P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭)) = RingHom.ker F := by
  set P₀ := MvPolynomial (Fin m) k with hP₀
  set Rq := Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 with hRq
  set I : Ideal P₀ := Ideal.under P₀ (RingHom.ker (F : Rq →+* Sq)) with hI
  have hkerI : Ideal.map (algebraMap P₀ Rq) I = RingHom.ker (F : Rq →+* Sq) :=
    IsLocalization.map_under 𝔭.primeCompl Rq _
  set T := P₀ ⧸ I with hT
  have hzero : ∀ x ∈ I, ((F : Rq →+* Sq).comp (algebraMap P₀ Rq)) x = 0 := by
    intro x hx
    simpa [hI, Ideal.under, RingHom.mem_ker] using hx
  let ψ : T →ₐ[k] Sq := Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ I (F.comp (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k P₀ Rq)) hzero
  let algTS : Algebra T Sq := (ψ : T →+* Sq).toAlgebra
  have hψ : ∀ x : T, ψ x = algebraMap T Sq x := fun x ↦ rfl
  have htsk : ∀ x : k, algebraMap k Sq x = algebraMap T Sq (algebraMap k T x) := fun x ↦ by
    rw [← hψ]; exact (ψ.commutes x).symm
  have : IsScalarTower k T Sq := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq htsk
  have hcomp :
    ∀ x : P₀, algebraMap T Sq (algebraMap P₀ T x) = (F : Rq →+* Sq) (algebraMap P₀ Rq x) := fun x ↦
    rfl
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap T Sq) := by
    rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
    intro a ha
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
    have hx : x ∈ I := by simpa [hI, Ideal.under, RingHom.mem_ker] using (hcomp x).symm.trans ha
    simpa using (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem (I := I)).mpr hx
  have hSloc : IsLocalization (Submonoid.map (algebraMap P₀ T) 𝔭.primeCompl) Sq := by
    refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rintro ⟨_, y, hy, rfl⟩
      rw [hcomp]
      exact (IsLocalization.map_units Rq ⟨y, hy⟩).map (F : Rq →+* Sq)
    · intro z
      obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := hF z
      obtain ⟨⟨x, s⟩, hxs⟩ := IsLocalization.surj 𝔭.primeCompl w
      refine ⟨⟨algebraMap P₀ T x, ⟨algebraMap P₀ T s, ⟨s, s.2, rfl⟩⟩⟩, ?_⟩
      rw [hcomp, hcomp]
      simp only [RingHom.coe_coe]
      rw [← map_mul, hxs]
    · intro x y hxy
      exact ⟨1, by rw [hinj hxy]⟩
  set p : Ideal T := (maximalIdeal Sq).comap (algebraMap T Sq) with hp
  have hpprime : p.IsPrime := inferInstance
  have : IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq p :=
    isLocalization_primeCompl_under (Submonoid.map (algebraMap P₀ T) 𝔭.primeCompl) hSloc
  have hae :
    (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ algebraMap P₀ T (MvPolynomial.X i)) : P₀ →ₐ[k] T) =
      IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k P₀ T := by
    apply MvPolynomial.algHom_ext
    intro i
    simp only [MvPolynomial.aeval_X]
    rfl
  let P : Algebra.Generators k T (Fin m) :=
    Algebra.Generators.ofSurjective (fun i ↦ algebraMap P₀ T (MvPolynomial.X i)) <| by
      rw [show
          (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ algebraMap P₀ T (MvPolynomial.X i)) : P₀ →ₐ[k] T) =
            IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k P₀ T
          from hae]
      exact Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hPmap : ∀ x : P.Ring, algebraMap P.Ring T x = algebraMap P₀ T x := by
    intro x
    rw [Algebra.Generators.algebraMap_apply]
    exact AlgHom.congr_fun hae x
  have hPker : P.ker = I := by
    have hk : P.ker = RingHom.ker (algebraMap P₀ T) := by
      refine Ideal.ext fun x ↦ ?_
      change algebraMap P.Ring T x = 0 ↔ algebraMap P₀ T x = 0
      rw [hPmap x]
    rw [hk, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq, Ideal.mk_ker]
  have hunder : p.comap (algebraMap P.Ring T) = 𝔭 := by
    have h1 : ((maximalIdeal Sq).comap (F : Rq →+* Sq)) = maximalIdeal Rq := by
      have hm := Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective (F : Rq →+* Sq) hF (K := maximalIdeal Sq)
      exact (IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal hm).symm ▸ rfl
    have h2 : (maximalIdeal Rq).comap (algebraMap P₀ Rq) = 𝔭 :=
      IsLocalization.AtPrime.under_maximalIdeal (S := Rq) (I := 𝔭)
    refine Ideal.ext fun x ↦ ?_
    rw [← h2, ← h1]
    simp only [Ideal.mem_comap, hp, hPmap x, hcomp x]
  have hpc : (p.comap (algebraMap P.Ring T)).primeCompl = 𝔭.primeCompl := by
    ext x
    simp only [Ideal.mem_primeCompl_iff, hunder]
  have : IsLocalization (p.comap (algebraMap P.Ring T)).primeCompl Rq := by
    rw [hpc]; infer_instance
  exact
    ⟨T, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, algTS, inferInstance, p, hpprime,
      inferInstance, P, inferInstance, by
      rw [hPker, show (algebraMap P.Ring Rq : P₀ →+* Rq) = algebraMap P₀ Rq from RingHom.ext fun x ↦
        rfl, hkerI, ker_coe_algHom F]⟩

/-- Suppose the local ring `S_q` of a finite type `k`-algebra `S`
is a quotient of a localization `k[y_1, …, y_m]_𝔭` of a polynomial ring at a prime by an ideal
generated by a regular sequence. Then `S_g` is a global complete intersection over `k` for some
`g ∉ q`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_of_exists_isRegular {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime]
    (Sq : Type*) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] [Algebra k Sq]
    [IsScalarTower k S Sq] {m : ℕ} {𝔭 : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)} [𝔭.IsPrime]
    (F : Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 →ₐ[k] Sq) (hF : Function.Surjective F)
    (hreg :
      ∃ rs : List (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭),
        IsRegular (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker F) :
    ∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g) := by
  have hlocSq : IsLocalRing Sq := IsLocalization.AtPrime.isLocalRing Sq q
  obtain ⟨T, _, _, _, _, _, p, _, _, P, _, hPker⟩ :=
    exists_generators_isLocalization_atPrime_of_surjective F hF
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq P p
  obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hker⟩ := hreg
  have htfae := (Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k T P p c hc
    (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭)).out 5 1
  obtain ⟨h, hh, hgci⟩ := htfae.mp ⟨rs, hrs, hker.trans hPker.symm⟩
  obtain ⟨_, _, p', _, _⟩ :=
    exists_isLocalization_atPrime_localizationAway (k := k) (T := T) (Sq := Sq) p hh
  exact exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_of_atPrime q Sq p' hgci

end CompleteIntersection

/-! ### Complete intersections at a prime -/

/-- Let `k` be a field, let `S` be a finite type `k`-algebra and let `q` be a
prime of `S`. Then: the local ring `S_q` is a complete intersection over `k`; `S_g` is a local
complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∉ q`; `S_g` is a global complete intersection over `k`
for some `g ∉ q`; and, for every presentation `S = k[x_i]/I` in finitely many variables, the
ideal `I_{q'}` of `k[x_i]_{q'}` is generated by a regular sequence — are all equivalent. -/
public theorem IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v)
    [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (Sq : Type*)
    [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] [Algebra k Sq]
    [IsScalarTower k S Sq] :
    List.TFAE
      [IsCompleteIntersection k Sq, ∃ g ∉ q, IsLocalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))],
          ∃ rs : List A,
            RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A rs ∧
              Ideal.ofList rs = P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)] := by
  have hlocSq : IsLocalRing Sq := IsLocalization.AtPrime.isLocalRing Sq q
  tfae_have 1 → 3 := by
    intro h1
    obtain ⟨R₀, hcr, hal, hrl, hef, fs, hfs, ⟨eqv⟩⟩ := h1
    let g₀ : R₀ →ₐ[k] Sq := (eqv.symm.toAlgHom).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k (Ideal.ofList fs))
    have hg₀s : Function.Surjective g₀ := eqv.symm.surjective.comp Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
    have hg₀ker : RingHom.ker g₀ = Ideal.ofList fs := by
      ext x
      simp only [RingHom.mem_ker]
      change eqv.symm (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList fs) x) = 0 ↔ x ∈ Ideal.ofList fs
      rw [map_eq_zero_iff _ eqv.symm.injective, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    obtain ⟨m, 𝔭, h𝔭, f₀, hf₀⟩ := CompleteIntersection.exists_atPrime_surjective k R₀
    have hrlB : IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) :=
      IsRegularRing.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization 𝔭 _
    refine
      CompleteIntersection.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_of_exists_isRegular q Sq
        (g₀.comp f₀) (hg₀s.comp hf₀) ?_
    have h00SE :=
      (IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae (f := (f₀ : Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 →+* R₀))
            (g := (g₀ : R₀ →+* Sq)) hf₀ hg₀s).out
        3 1
    obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hrsker⟩ :=
      h00SE.mp ⟨fs, hfs, by rw [CompleteIntersection.ker_coe_algHom g₀, hg₀ker]⟩
    exact ⟨rs, hrs, by rw [hrsker, CompleteIntersection.ker_comp_coe_algHom g₀ f₀]⟩
  tfae_have 3 → 2 := by
    rintro ⟨g, hg, hgci⟩
    exact ⟨g, hg, hgci.isLocalCompleteIntersection⟩
  tfae_have 2 → 3 := by
    rintro ⟨g, hg, hlci⟩
    obtain ⟨algL, twrL, pL, hpL, hlocL⟩ :=
      CompleteIntersection.exists_isLocalization_atPrime_localizationAway (k := k) (T := S) (Sq :=
        Sq) q hg
    obtain ⟨h, hh, hgci⟩ := hlci.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection hpL.ne_top
    obtain ⟨algM, twrM, pM, hpM, hlocM⟩ :=
      CompleteIntersection.exists_isLocalization_atPrime_localizationAway (k := k) (T :=
        Localization.Away g) (Sq := Sq) pL hh
    exact CompleteIntersection.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_of_atPrime q Sq pM hgci
  tfae_have 3 → 4 := by
    intro h3 ι _ P A _ _ _
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq P q
    exact
      ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc A).out 1 5).mp h3
  tfae_have 4 → 3 := by
    intro h4
    obtain ⟨n, f, hf⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial''.mp ‹Algebra.FiniteType k S›
    let e := MvPolynomial.renameEquiv k (Equiv.ulift (α := Fin n)).symm
    let F : MvPolynomial (ULift.{w} (Fin n)) k →ₐ[k] S := f.comp (e.symm : _ →ₐ[k] _)
    have hFs : Function.Surjective F := hf.comp e.symm.surjective
    have hFe :
      (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ F (MvPolynomial.X i)) :
          MvPolynomial (ULift.{w} (Fin n)) k →ₐ[k] S) =
        F :=
      MvPolynomial.algHom_ext (by simp)
    let P : Algebra.Generators k S (ULift.{w} (Fin n)) :=
      Algebra.Generators.ofSurjective (fun i ↦ F (MvPolynomial.X i))
        (by
          rw [hFe]; exact hFs)
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq P q
    exact
      ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc
                (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)))).out
            5 1).mp
        (h4 (ULift.{w} (Fin n)) P (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))))
  tfae_have 3 → 1 := by
    intro h3
    obtain ⟨n, f, hf⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial''.mp ‹Algebra.FiniteType k S›
    have hfe :
      (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ f (MvPolynomial.X i)) : MvPolynomial (Fin n) k →ₐ[k] S) = f :=
      MvPolynomial.algHom_ext (by simp)
    let P : Algebra.Generators k S (Fin n) :=
      Algebra.Generators.ofSurjective (fun i ↦ f (MvPolynomial.X i))
        (by
          rw [hfe]; exact hf)
    have hq'p : (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
    have hrlA : IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))) :=
      IsRegularRing.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)) _
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq P q
    obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hrsker⟩ :=
      ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc
                (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)))).out
            1 5).mp
        h3
    obtain ⟨θ, hθ, hθker⟩ :=
      CompleteIntersection.exists_surjective_algHom_ker_eq_map_ker (k := k) (R := P.Ring)
        P.algebraMap_surjective q (Localization.AtPrime (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))) Sq
    exact
      isCompleteIntersection_of_ker_eq_ofList hθ hrs
        (by
          rw [hrsker, hθker]; rfl)
  tfae_finish

/-- Let `k` be a field, let `S` be a finite type `k`-algebra and let `q` be a prime of `S`. The
following are equivalent:

1. the local ring `S_q` is a complete intersection over `k`;
2. `S_g` is a local complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∈ S`, `g ∉ q`;
3. `S_g` is a global complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∈ S`, `g ∉ q`;
4. for every presentation `S = k[x_i]/I` in finitely many variables, with `q' ⊆ k[x_i]` the prime
   corresponding to `q` and `c` the codimension, `height q' = height q + c`, all of the equivalent
   conditions (1)-(5) of Stacks 00SC hold: `S_g` is a global complete intersection for some
   `g ∉ q`; `I_{q'}` is generated by `c` elements; the conormal module of `I_{q'}` is generated
   by `c` elements; it is free of rank `c`; and `I_{q'}` is generated by a regular sequence in
   `k[x_i]_{q'}`.

Entries 5-9 of the list are item (4) with a single one of the conditions (1)-(5) of 00SC, in
order: for every presentation, that one condition holds. -/
@[stacks 00SG "Item (1) is `IsCompleteIntersection k Sq` for an abstract localization `Sq` of `S`
at `q`, with the `k`-algebra structure induced from `S`; items (2) and (3) use
`Localization.Away g`, as Definition 00S9 does. Item (4) is entry 4 of the `List.TFAE`: for every
presentation `Algebra.Generators k S ι` with `ι` finite, every localization `A` of `k[x_i]` at
`q'` and every `c : ℕ` with `height q' = height q + c` (the source's `c`, which exists by
`Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq`), the conjunction of conditions (1)-(5) of Lemma 00SC
in the form of `Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away`. Entries 5-9 state
item (4) for each one of the conditions (1)-(5) of 00SC separately, so item (4) holds whichever
of the equivalent conditions is chosen. See the module docstring.", ega "IV 19.3.2" "special case"]
public theorem IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae_generators (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (S : Type v) [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime]
    (Sq : Type*) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] [Algebra k Sq]
    [IsScalarTower k S Sq] :
    List.TFAE
      [IsCompleteIntersection k Sq, ∃ g ∉ q, IsLocalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))] (c : ℕ),
          (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c →
            (∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g)) ∧
            Submodule.spanFinrank (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)) ≤ c ∧
            (⊤ : Submodule (A ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A))
                (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)).Cotangent).spanFinrank ≤ c ∧
            (Module.Free (A ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A))
                (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)).Cotangent ∧
              Module.finrank (A ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A))
                (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)).Cotangent = c) ∧
            ∃ rs : List A,
              RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A rs ∧
                Ideal.ofList rs = P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A),
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))] (c : ℕ),
          (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c →
            ∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))] (c : ℕ),
          (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c →
            Submodule.spanFinrank (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)) ≤ c,
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))] (c : ℕ),
          (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c →
            (⊤ : Submodule (A ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A))
                (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)).Cotangent).spanFinrank ≤ c,
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))] (c : ℕ),
          (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c →
            Module.Free (A ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A))
                (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)).Cotangent ∧
              Module.finrank (A ⧸ P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A))
                (P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)).Cotangent = c,
        ∀ (ι : Type w) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k S ι) (A : Type (max u w)) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S))] (c : ℕ),
          (q.comap (algebraMap P.Ring S)).height = q.height + c →
            ∃ rs : List A,
              RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular A rs ∧
                Ideal.ofList rs = P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)] := by
  have old := IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae.{u, v, w} k S q Sq
  tfae_have 1 ↔ 2 := old.out 1 2
  tfae_have 1 ↔ 3 := old.out 1 3
  tfae_have 3 → 4 := by
    intro h3 ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    have T := Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc A
    exact ⟨h3, (T.out 1 2).mp h3, (T.out 1 3).mp h3, (T.out 1 4).mp h3, (T.out 1 5).mp h3⟩
  tfae_have 4 → 5 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact (h ι P A c hc).1
  tfae_have 4 → 6 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact (h ι P A c hc).2.1
  tfae_have 4 → 7 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact (h ι P A c hc).2.2.1
  tfae_have 4 → 8 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact (h ι P A c hc).2.2.2.1
  tfae_have 4 → 9 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact (h ι P A c hc).2.2.2.2
  tfae_have 5 → 9 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc A).out 1 5).mp
      (h ι P A c hc)
  tfae_have 6 → 9 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc A).out 2 5).mp
      (h ι P A c hc)
  tfae_have 7 → 9 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc A).out 3 5).mp
      (h ι P A c hc)
  tfae_have 8 → 9 := by
    intro h ι _ P A _ _ _ c hc
    exact ((Algebra.Generators.tfae_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_away k S P q c hc A).out 4 5).mp
      (h ι P A c hc)
  tfae_have 9 → 3 := by
    intro h
    refine (old.out 4 3).mp ?_
    intro ι _ P A _ _ _
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Algebra.Generators.exists_height_comap_eq P q
    exact h ι P A c hc
  tfae_finish

/-! ### Local complete intersections -/

/-- A `k`-algebra `S` is a local complete intersection over `k` if and only if every maximal ideal
`m` of `S` admits a `g ∉ m` with `S_g` a global complete intersection over `k`. -/
theorem isLocalCompleteIntersection_iff_forall_isMaximal {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v}
    [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] :
    IsLocalCompleteIntersection k S ↔
      ∀ m : Ideal S, m.IsMaximal → ∃ g ∉ m, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g) :=
  ⟨fun hS m hm ↦ hS.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection hm.ne_top, fun h ↦ by
    refine ⟨{g : S | IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g)}, ?_, fun g hg ↦ hg⟩
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ hne
    obtain ⟨g, hgm, hgci⟩ := h m hm
    exact hgm (hle (Ideal.subset_span hgci))⟩

namespace Stacks.CompleteIntersection.LocalRings

/-- A localization `S_q` of `S` at a prime `q` is a complete intersection over `k` if and only if
`S_g` is a global complete intersection over `k` for some `g ∉ q`. -/
private theorem isCompleteIntersection_iff_exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection (k : Type u)
    [Field k] (S : Type v) [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (q : Ideal S)
    [q.IsPrime] (Sq : Type w) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q]
    [Algebra k Sq] [IsScalarTower k S Sq] :
    IsCompleteIntersection k Sq ↔ ∃ g ∉ q, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g) :=
  (IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae.{u, v, 0, w} k S q Sq).out 1 3

end Stacks.CompleteIntersection.LocalRings

/-- Let `k` be a field and let `S` be a finite type `k`-algebra. Then: `S` is a
local complete intersection over `k`; every local ring of `S` is a complete intersection over
`k`; and every localization of `S` at a maximal ideal is a complete intersection over `k` — are
all equivalent. The local rings in the last two items are abstract localizations of `S`, carrying
the `k`-algebra structure induced from `S`. -/
@[stacks 00SH "Item (1) is `IsLocalCompleteIntersection k S` (Definition 00S9 (2)), and items (2)
and (3) say that `IsCompleteIntersection k Sq` (Definition 00SD) holds for every localization of
`S` at a prime, resp. at a maximal ideal, quantified over abstract localizations `Sq` in the
universe of `S` with the `k`-algebra structure induced from `S` — the hypothesis block of item
(1) of Lemma 00SG. The source's finite type hypothesis is kept: items (2) and (3) do not imply
it, as `ℚ(x)` over `ℚ` shows. The source's appeal to quasi-compactness of `Spec S` is absent,
`IsLocalCompleteIntersection` asking for a covering by an arbitrary set of elements generating
the unit ideal. See the module docstring."]
public theorem IsLocalCompleteIntersection.tfae (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v) [CommRing S]
    [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] :
    List.TFAE
      [IsLocalCompleteIntersection k S,
        ∀ (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (Sq : Type v) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq]
          [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] [Algebra k Sq] [IsScalarTower k S Sq],
          IsCompleteIntersection k Sq,
        ∀ (m : Ideal S) [m.IsMaximal] (Sm : Type v) [CommRing Sm] [Algebra S Sm]
          [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sm m] [Algebra k Sm] [IsScalarTower k S Sm],
          IsCompleteIntersection k Sm] := by
  open Stacks.CompleteIntersection.LocalRings in
  tfae_have 1 → 2 := by
    intro hS q _ Sq _ _ _ _ _
    exact
      (isCompleteIntersection_iff_exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection k S q Sq).mpr
        (hS.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection ‹q.IsPrime›.ne_top)
  tfae_have 2 → 3 := by
    intro h m hm Sm _ _ _ _ _
    have := hm.isPrime
    exact h m Sm
  tfae_have 3 → 1 := fun h ↦
    isLocalCompleteIntersection_iff_forall_isMaximal.mpr fun m hm ↦
      have := hm.isPrime
      (isCompleteIntersection_iff_exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection k S m
            (Localization.AtPrime m)).mp
        (h m (Localization.AtPrime m))
  tfae_finish

namespace Stacks.CompleteIntersection.LocalRings

/-- For a finite type `k`-algebra `S`, the following are equivalent: `S` is a local complete
intersection over `k`; every local ring of `S` is a complete intersection over `k`; and every
localization of `S` at a maximal ideal is a complete intersection over `k`.

Alias of `IsLocalCompleteIntersection.tfae`. -/
public alias solution := _root_.IsLocalCompleteIntersection.tfae

end Stacks.CompleteIntersection.LocalRings

/-! ### Complete intersections among local rings essentially of finite type -/

namespace Stacks.CompleteIntersection.Independence

open RingTheory.Sequence IsLocalRing

section Helpers

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S]

/-- Being generated by a regular sequence is carried across an isomorphism of the source: if
`g ∘ e = f` for an isomorphism `e` of `k`-algebras, a regular sequence generating `Ker g`
produces one generating `Ker f`. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ker_of_algEquiv {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra k A] [Algebra k B] (e : A ≃ₐ[k] B) {f : A →ₐ[k] S} {g : B →ₐ[k] S}
    (hfg : ∀ x, g (e x) = f x)
    (h : ∃ rs : List B, IsRegular B rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker g) :
    ∃ rs : List A, IsRegular A rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker f := by
  obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hker⟩ := h
  let φ : B →+* A := (e.symm : B →ₐ[k] A).toRingHom
  have hφ : ∀ b, e (φ b) = b := fun b ↦ e.apply_symm_apply b
  refine ⟨rs.map φ, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine
      (AddEquiv.isRegular_congr (e := (e.symm : B ≃+* A).toAddEquiv)
            (List.forall₂_map_right_iff.mpr (List.forall₂_same.mpr fun r _ x ↦ ?_))).mp
        hrs
    simp [φ, smul_eq_mul]
  · rw [← Ideal.map_ofList φ, hker]
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
      intro b hb
      have hb' : f (φ b) = g b := by rw [← hfg (φ b), hφ b]
      simpa only [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker, hb'] using hb
    · intro a ha
      have hea : e a ∈ RingHom.ker g := by
        rw [RingHom.mem_ker, hfg a]; exact ha
      have haφ : a = φ (e a) := (e.symm_apply_apply a).symm
      rw [haφ]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem φ hea

/-- A local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type over `k` is the localization at a prime of a
quotient of a polynomial ring over `k`, hence of a `k`-algebra of finite type carried by a type
in the universe of `k`. -/
@[ega "IV 1.3.11" "base ring is a field"]
private theorem exists_finiteType_isLocalization_atPrime (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v)
    [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (J : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k)) (_ : Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ J) S) (_
      : IsScalarTower k (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ J) S) (p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ J)) (_
      : p.IsPrime), IsLocalization.AtPrime S p :=
  _root_.CompleteIntersection.exists_finiteType_isLocalization_atPrime k S

/-- A local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type over `k` is a quotient of a localization of a
polynomial ring over `k` at a prime. -/
@[ega "IV 1.3.11" "base ring is a field"]
private theorem exists_atPrime_surjective (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v) [CommRing S]
    [Algebra k S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (q : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k)) (_ : q.IsPrime) (f :
      Localization.AtPrime q →ₐ[k] S), Function.Surjective f :=
  _root_.CompleteIntersection.exists_atPrime_surjective k S

/-- `IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae` with the presentations of item (4) indexed
by types in `Type`. -/
private theorem localization_atPrime_tfae₀ (k : Type u) [Field k] (T : Type u₂) [CommRing T]
    [Algebra k T] [Algebra.FiniteType k T] (p : Ideal T) [p.IsPrime] (S : Type v) [CommRing S]
    [Algebra T S] [IsLocalization.AtPrime S p] [Algebra k S] [IsScalarTower k T S] :
    List.TFAE
      [IsCompleteIntersection k S, ∃ g ∉ p, IsLocalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∃ g ∉ p, IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k (Localization.Away g),
        ∀ (ι : Type) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k T ι) (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
          [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (p.comap (algebraMap P.Ring T))],
          ∃ rs : List A, IsRegular A rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A)] :=
  IsCompleteIntersection.localization_atPrime_tfae k T p S

/-- If `S` is a complete intersection over `k`, the kernel of any
surjection onto `S` from a localization of a polynomial ring over `k` at a prime is generated by
a regular sequence. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ker_of_isCompleteIntersection [IsLocalRing S]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] {n : ℕ} {q : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k)} [q.IsPrime]
    (f : Localization.AtPrime q →ₐ[k] S) (hf : Function.Surjective f)
    (h : IsCompleteIntersection k S) :
    ∃ rs : List (Localization.AtPrime q),
      IsRegular (Localization.AtPrime q) rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker f := by
  obtain ⟨T, _, _, _, _, _, p, _, _, P, _, hPker⟩ :=
    CompleteIntersection.exists_generators_isLocalization_atPrime_of_surjective f hf
  have h14 :
    ∀ (ι : Type) [Finite ι] (P : Algebra.Generators k T ι) (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
      [Algebra P.Ring A] [IsLocalization.AtPrime A (p.comap (algebraMap P.Ring T))],
      ∃ rs : List A, IsRegular A rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = P.ker.map (algebraMap P.Ring A) :=
    ((localization_atPrime_tfae₀ k T p S).out 1 4).mp h
  obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hrsker⟩ := h14 (Fin n) P (Localization.AtPrime q)
  exact ⟨rs, hrs, hrsker.trans hPker⟩

/-- A complete intersection over `k` is a local ring of a global complete
intersection over `k`, with the global complete intersection taken in the universe of `k`. -/
private theorem exists_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_atPrime [IsLocalRing S]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] (h : IsCompleteIntersection k S) :
    ∃ (A : Type u) (_ : CommRing A) (_ : Algebra k A) (_ : Algebra A S) (_ : IsScalarTower k A S)
      (a : Ideal A) (_ : a.IsPrime),
      IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k A ∧ IsLocalization.AtPrime S a := by
  obtain ⟨n, J, algTS, twr, p, hp, hL⟩ :=
    exists_finiteType_isLocalization_atPrime k S
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hgci⟩ := ((localization_atPrime_tfae₀ k _ p S).out 1 3).mp h
  obtain ⟨algL, twrL, p', hp', hlocL⟩ :=
    CompleteIntersection.exists_isLocalization_atPrime_localizationAway (k := k) (Sq := S) p hg
  exact ⟨_, inferInstance, inferInstance, algL, twrL, p', hp', hgci, hlocL⟩

/-- A local ring of a local complete intersection over `k` is a complete intersection over `k`. -/
private theorem isCompleteIntersection_of_isLocalCompleteIntersection [IsLocalRing S] {A : Type*}
    [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [Algebra A S] [IsScalarTower k A S] (a : Ideal A) [ha : a.IsPrime]
    [IsLocalization.AtPrime S a] (h : IsLocalCompleteIntersection k A) :
    IsCompleteIntersection k S := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hgci⟩ := h.exists_notMem_isGlobalCompleteIntersection ha.ne_top
  have : Algebra.FiniteType k (Localization.Away g) := hgci.finiteType
  obtain ⟨algL, twrL, p, hp, hlocL⟩ :=
    CompleteIntersection.exists_isLocalization_atPrime_localizationAway (k := k) (Sq := S) a hg
  have h31 := (localization_atPrime_tfae₀ k (Localization.Away g) p S).out 3 1
  exact h31.mp ⟨1, fun h1 ↦ hp.ne_top ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one p).mpr h1),
    isGlobalCompleteIntersection_localization k _ 1 hgci⟩

/-- Being essentially of finite type over `k` is carried across an isomorphism of
`k`-algebras. -/
private theorem essFiniteType_of_algEquiv {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra k A]
    [Algebra k B] (e : A ≃ₐ[k] B) [Algebra.EssFiniteType k A] : Algebra.EssFiniteType k B :=
  (Algebra.EssFiniteType.iff_of_algEquiv e).mp ‹_›

end Helpers

end Stacks.CompleteIntersection.Independence

/-- Let `k` be a field and let `S` be a local `k`-algebra essentially of finite
type over `k`. The following are equivalent: `S` is a complete intersection over `k`; for every
surjection `f : R →ₐ[k] S` with `R` a regular local `k`-algebra essentially of finite type over
`k` the ideal `Ker f` is generated by a regular sequence; for some such surjection `Ker f` is
generated by `dim R - dim S` elements; `S` is a localization of a global complete intersection
over `k` at a prime; and `S` is a localization of a local complete intersection over `k` at a
prime.

`Generated by dim R - dim S elements` is the additive equality
`dim S + spanFinrank (Ker f) = dim R`, and items (4) and (5) exhibit `S` as a localization by an
instance rather than by an isomorphism with `Localization.AtPrime`. -/
@[stacks 00SF "Items (1)-(5) are the five items of the list, in the source's order. `Essentially
of finite presentation over k` is `Algebra.EssFiniteType k R`, the two notions agreeing over a
field; the source's proof states item (2) with `essentially of finite type` as well. `Generated
by dim R - dim S elements` is `ringKrullDim S + (RingHom.ker f).spanFinrank = ringKrullDim R`,
the reading of Lemma 00SE: subtraction in `WithBot ℕ∞` is truncated while the inequality `≥`
holds unconditionally, so the equality says the minimal number of generators attains
`dim R - dim S`. In items (4) and (5) the isomorphism `S ≅ A_𝔞` is stated abstractly, as
`IsLocalization.AtPrime S a` for an `A`-algebra structure on `S` compatible with `k`. Item (2)
quantifies over rings in `Type (max u w)` for a universe parameter `w`: that asserts it in every
universe and still lets it be instantiated at the localization `k[x_1, …, x_n]_𝔮` of the source's
proof of (2) ⇒ (1), which a free `Type w` would not. The existential items (3)-(5) put their
witnesses in the universe of `k`, where the source's are. The hypothesis that the surjections be
local ring homomorphisms is omitted, being a consequence of surjectivity. See the module
docstring.", ega "IV 19.3.2" "ess. f.t. over a field"]
public theorem IsCompleteIntersection.tfae (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type v) [CommRing S]
    [Algebra k S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S] :
    List.TFAE
      [IsCompleteIntersection k S,
        ∀ (R : Type (max u w)) (_ : CommRing R) (_ : Algebra k R) (_ : IsRegularLocalRing R)
          (_ : Algebra.EssFiniteType k R) (f : R →ₐ[k] S),
          Function.Surjective f →
            ∃ rs : List R, RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker f,
        ∃ (R : Type u) (_ : CommRing R) (_ : Algebra k R) (_ : IsRegularLocalRing R) (_ :
          Algebra.EssFiniteType k R) (f : R →ₐ[k] S),
          Function.Surjective f ∧ ringKrullDim S + (RingHom.ker f).spanFinrank = ringKrullDim R,
        ∃ (A : Type u) (_ : CommRing A) (_ : Algebra k A) (_ : Algebra A S) (_ :
          IsScalarTower k A S) (a : Ideal A) (_ : a.IsPrime),
          IsGlobalCompleteIntersection k A ∧ IsLocalization.AtPrime S a,
        ∃ (A : Type u) (_ : CommRing A) (_ : Algebra k A) (_ : Algebra A S) (_ :
          IsScalarTower k A S) (a : Ideal A) (_ : a.IsPrime),
          IsLocalCompleteIntersection k A ∧ IsLocalization.AtPrime S a] := by
  open Stacks.CompleteIntersection.Independence in
  tfae_have 1 → 3 := by
    rintro ⟨R, iR, iRk, ireg, iess, fs, hfs, ⟨e⟩⟩
    let F : R →ₐ[k] S := e.symm.toAlgHom.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k (Ideal.ofList fs))
    have hFs : Function.Surjective F := e.symm.surjective.comp Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
    have hker : RingHom.ker ((F : R →+* S)) = Ideal.ofList fs := by
      ext x
      simp [F, RingHom.mem_ker, map_eq_zero_iff _ e.symm.injective, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    refine ⟨R, iR, iRk, ireg, iess, F, hFs, ?_⟩
    have h :=
      IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae (A := R) (B := R) (C := S) (f := RingHom.id R)
        (g := (F : R →+* S)) Function.surjective_id hFs
    have h3 : ∃ rs : List R, IsRegular R rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (F : R →+* S) :=
      ⟨fs, hfs, hker.symm⟩
    have h34 := (h.out 3 4).mp h3
    rw [← CompleteIntersection.ker_coe_algHom F]
    exact h34
  tfae_have 3 → 1 := by
    rintro ⟨R, iR, iRk, ireg, iess, f, hf, hdim⟩
    have h :=
      IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae (A := R) (B := R) (C := S) (f := RingHom.id R)
        (g := (f : R →+* S)) Function.surjective_id hf
    rw [← CompleteIntersection.ker_coe_algHom f] at hdim
    obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hker⟩ := (h.out 4 3).mp hdim
    rw [CompleteIntersection.ker_coe_algHom f] at hker
    exact
      isCompleteIntersection_of_ker_eq_ofList hf hrs hker
  tfae_have 1 → 4 := exists_isGlobalCompleteIntersection_atPrime
  tfae_have 4 → 5 := by
    rintro ⟨A, i1, i2, i3, i4, a, ha, hgci, hloc⟩
    exact
      ⟨A, i1, i2, i3, i4, a, ha, hgci.isLocalCompleteIntersection,
        hloc⟩
  tfae_have 5 → 2 := by
    rintro ⟨A, i1, i2, i3, i4, a, ha, hlci, hloc⟩ R iR iRk ireg iess f hf
    have h1 : IsCompleteIntersection k S :=
      isCompleteIntersection_of_isLocalCompleteIntersection a hlci
    obtain ⟨n, q, hq, ψ, hψ⟩ := exists_atPrime_surjective k R
    have hrs := exists_isRegular_ker_of_isCompleteIntersection (f.comp ψ) (hf.comp hψ) h1
    rw [← CompleteIntersection.ker_comp_coe_algHom f ψ] at hrs
    have h :=
      IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isRegular_ker_tfae (A := Localization.AtPrime q) (B := R) (C := S)
        (f := (ψ : Localization.AtPrime q →+* R)) (g := (f : R →+* S)) hψ hf
    have h13 := (h.out 1 3).mp hrs
    rw [← CompleteIntersection.ker_coe_algHom f]
    exact h13
  tfae_have 2 → 1 := by
    intro h2
    obtain ⟨n, q, hq, φ, hφ⟩ := exists_atPrime_surjective k S
    have iess : Algebra.EssFiniteType k (ULift.{w} (Localization.AtPrime q)) :=
      essFiniteType_of_algEquiv (ULift.algEquiv (R := k)).symm
    have ireg : IsRegularLocalRing (ULift.{w} (Localization.AtPrime q)) :=
      IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv (ULift.ringEquiv).symm
    have h :=
      h2 (ULift.{w} (Localization.AtPrime q)) inferInstance inferInstance ireg iess
        (φ.comp (ULift.algEquiv (R := k)).toAlgHom) (hφ.comp (ULift.algEquiv (R := k)).surjective)
    obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hker⟩ :=
      exists_isRegular_ker_of_algEquiv (ULift.algEquiv (R := k)).symm (f := φ) (g :=
        φ.comp (ULift.algEquiv (R := k)).toAlgHom) (fun x ↦ by simp) h
    exact
      isCompleteIntersection_of_ker_eq_ofList hφ hrs hker
  tfae_finish

namespace Stacks.CompleteIntersection.Independence

/-- For a local `k`-algebra `S` essentially of finite type, the following are equivalent: `S` is a
complete intersection over `k`; the kernel of every surjection onto `S` from a regular local
`k`-algebra essentially of finite type is generated by a regular sequence; for some such
surjection `f : R →ₐ[k] S`, `dim S + spanFinrank (Ker f) = dim R`; and `S` is a localization at a
prime of a global, resp. local, complete intersection over `k`.

Alias of `IsCompleteIntersection.tfae`. -/
public alias solution := _root_.IsCompleteIntersection.tfae

end Stacks.CompleteIntersection.Independence

